    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** serving as the anchor of the offense, boasting a strong 68.55 score. Facing Sonny Gray, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable dynamic platoon split (+14%) and the premium protection of the #3 spot in the lineup, making him the highest-ceiling play in a day where few matchups offer elite offensive environments. While **Jackson Merrill** faces a stiff test against Kevin Gausman, his 57.69 score keeps him in the marginal-to-strong range, bolstered by a +13% platoon adjustment that offsets the pitcher\u2019s skill level. Meanwhile, the top of the lineup sees **Sam Antonacci** leading off against Hunter Brown; his 52.33 score is driven largely by his placement at the top of the order (+10%) and a positive platoon edge, providing the requisite table-setting potential we need to chase our scarcity targets in stolen bases.\n\nOur bench decisions today were dictated largely by inactivity, as **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are all sitting on off-days, effectively forcing our hand. **Drake Baldwin** is the most precarious start of the day at 47.27; despite batting second, his score is depressed by a significant -19% penalty due to the elite xERA of Cristopher S\u00e1nchez. We are essentially relying on his position in the order to generate counting stats, as the raw matchup is the toughest on our board. We remain cautious with **Miguel Vargas** (48.18) against Hunter Brown; while his xwOBA is respectable, he lacks the speed-based upside we prioritize, placing him on the lower end of our active rotation. We are monitoring **Luis Robert Jr.** closely, as he remains sidelined on the IL, further limiting our ability to rotate in high-upside speed assets like **Nasim Nunez** or **Brayan Rocchio** should the lineup flow stagnate.",
